al contract  to that contractor that is a classic  quid pro quo illegal quid pro quo  arrangements also tend to pop up in a  workplace setting a quid pro quo would  exist where an employer demands sexual  favors in return for an employee keeping  their job so it depends on the context  Mick Mulvaney has recently been  emphasizing that especially in foreign  policy settings quid pro quo  arrangements happen all the time that's  just the nature of foreign policy we do  that all the time with foreign policy  I'll help you do this if you help me do  that everyone is happy and secure for  example throughout the history of the  United States we have used our own aid  or assistance as leverage for achieving  things such as democracy abroad an end  to corruption and even physical access  to important geographical areas for  example President Jimmy Carter provided  Egypt with aid in exchange for Egypt  making peace with Israel President Bush  even demanded that countries provide  free speech and freedom of assembly  before receiving certain US aid however  while this may be true quid pro quos  that involve a concerted self-interest  for a particular politician do not  happen all the time in foreign policy  quite frankly they really don't happen  at all in fact it was such a stunning  admission by Mick Mulvaney to admit that  this was a quid pro quo on behalf of the  Trump administration ostensibly for  president Trump that it elicited an  almost immediate walk back from Mulvaney  and the rest of the administration this  arrangement between the Trump  administration and President zalenski of  Ukraine falls into the problematic  category of quid pro quos for a couple  of reasons first of all such an  arrangement is probably highly illegal  and may be sufficient to prove the  crimes of bribery and election  interference well would be admittedly  difficult to indict and convict a  president of these crimes for reasons  that we've already talked about on this  channel in order to establish a prima  facie case for bribery under 18 USC 201  one would have to prove that a public  official in this case president Trump  directly or indirectly corruptly  demanded anything of value personally  in this case bolstering his re-election  campaign in return for being influenced  in the performance of any official act  in this case releasing money that  Congress in the Pentagon had already  appropriated for Ukraine or you can take  for example 51 USC three zero one two  one which states that it shall be  unlawful for a foreign national directly  or indirectly to make a contribution or  donation of money or other thing of  value or to make an express or implied  promise to make a contribution or  donation in connection with a federal  state or local election in this case one  would argue that the thing of value is  investigating a political rival which  obviously the Trump administration would  try to lord over the head of Joe Biden  as he tries to secure the Democratic  nomination for potentially running for  president of United States in 2020  additionally an apart from whether any  of these acts fit the neat statutory  definitions of these crimes and overcome  the constitutional issues in terms of in  dining a sitting president this  arrangement is problematic because it  essentially means that the President of  the United States is subverting the  national interest for his own personal  interest in other words he's putting  himself above the entire country now no  one argues that hunter Biden's status as  a board member of Purisima doesn't smack  of nepotism  but strong-arming a sovereign nation  into investigating a conspiracy theory  about ukrainian computer servers and  shinning up a defunct investigation into  buries m'a appears to serve president  Trump only and not US national interest  it appears motivated primarily if not  solely to help President Trump get  reelected and not to help America Rudy  Giuliani tweets the quiet part out loud  when he tweeted with all the fake news  let me make it clear that everything I  did was to discover evidence to defend  my client against false charges  Dems would be horrified by the attacks  on me if my client was a terrorist but  they don't believe real Donald Trump has  rights the problem here is that at the  request of the president Rudy Giuliani  was running his own shadow foreign  policy operation and he's admitting that  in this context he wasn't acting on  behalf of America but acting on behalf  of his client  Donald Trump in trying to get dirt  against a political rival if this had  been in America's interest President  Trump would have used the usual  diplomatic channels gone through the  mutual legal assistance treaty and  avoided using an entirely separate  clandestine shadow foreign policy team  led by Rudy Giuliani this kind of  arrangement pressuring Ukraine to do  something to benefit president Trump  personally in exchange for four hundred  million dollars in US aid and assistance  is what appears to be an abuse of power  and an attempt to use one's official  capacity as president for personal gain  now some including former acting  Attorney General Matthew Whitaker have  argued that an abuse of power is not a  crime what evidence of a crime you have  I mean the Constitution you know sort of  abuse of power is not a crime the  Constitution is very clear that this has  to be some pretty egregious behavior  however such an abuse of power is a  crucial inquiry as far as impeachment is  concerned that's because impeachment was  designed to dismantle this kind of abuse  of power ironically Bill Taylor came out  of retirement at the request of Mike  Pompeo to help Ukraine now he'll  probably want to go back into retirement  and now that he has more time on his  hands maybe he'll finally listened to  his grandkids and join Instagram after  taking Brandon Wolfe falls class  instagram-worthy photography shoot edit  and share or maybe he will finally  tackle all those chores around the house  his wife asked him to do like  redesigning his family room he could  really use Emily Henderson's Skillshare  class style your space creative tips and  techniques for interior design  Skillshare is an online learning  community that has tens of thousands of  classes on everything like music design  lifestyle and technology it's great for  former top diplomats who suddenly find  themselves with a lot more time on their  hands a yearly membership is less than  $10 per month but legal eagles will get  two free months of Skillshare when you  click on the link below plus it really  helps out this channel the free premium  membership gives you unlimited access to  must know topics so you can prove your  skills and learn new things all free for  two months so improve yourself now while  you're waiting to give your own  congressional testimony before the house  impeachment inquiry do you agree with my  analysis leave your objections in the  comments and check out my other real law  reviews over here where I talk about the  whistleblower hearsay objections to the  impeachment  in tons of other breaking news and as  always I will see you in court
 

